  - learning-analytics
  - gamification
abstract: >-
  JSVerseHub is an open-source, browser-based platform for learning JavaScript, organised as a galaxy of
  fifteen concept modules with authored explanations, runnable examples, exercises and quizzes. It is written
  in framework-free ES2022 JavaScript and bundles each concept as a lazily loaded chunk. The platform includes
  an SM-2 spaced-repetition scheduler, a Bayesian Knowledge Tracing learner model and an xAPI-inspired
  learning-analytics log, all of which run entirely on the learner's device with an anonymous actor
  identifier and can be exported as JSON or CSV for offline analysis.
